    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Program Format:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Full-time, four-year program."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Admission Information",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Admission Information",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/fcad/professional_music/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "O.S.S.D. with six Grade 12 U/M courses including Grade 12 U English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Notes:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "ENG4U/EAE4U is the preferred English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "A grade of 70 percent or higher will be required in Grade 12 U English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "As part of the admission selection process, applicants must visit the Program page for details about the non-academic requirements.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Program",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/content/ryerson/programs/undergraduate/professional-music/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Admission decisions are made based on meeting the academic requirements, and an assessment of the Non-Academic Requirements (resume, music production demo or business executive summary, written statement, and reference forms) by the Professional Music program department."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "A non-academic assessment fee of $50 CAD (non-refundable and subject to change) is required."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Subject to competition, candidates may be required to present averages/grades above the minimum."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Program Overview/Curriculum Information",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Program Overview/Curriculum Information",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/fcad/professional_music/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The Professional Music BFA is a unique four-year undergraduate program located in the heart of Toronto. The cross-disciplinary program enrols students in courses that include studio and live production, music fundamentals and the business of music."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The curriculum is designed to prepare the modern music-minded person for a career in digital audio recording, live entertainment, entrepreneurship and a variety of other music industry positions. Professional Music will equip students with the skills necessary for the ever-evolving music industry, providing an experiential learning environment in the centre of Canada’s music industry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Learning Outcomes"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Theoretically describe digital music production and creative production requirements and apply those principles within a digital music production context."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Theoretically describe the concepts and relationships between melody, harmony, and rhythm, the fundamental aspects of musicianship, and apply those relationships in a digital music production context."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Theoretically describe the concepts and the implications of music and media business practices and instruments including contracts, negotiation, financial documents, sales & marketing, and apply those insights and processes in a music industry and entrepreneurial context."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Theoretically describe and apply digital media production skills and requirements."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Draw on existing skills through self-awareness, awareness of context, and theory to engage in entrepreneurial practices, risks, and opportunities."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Professionally communicate verbally, in writing and other media."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Be sensitive and open to diversity in terms of people and cultures, with consideration of specific issues of equity, social justice, and inclusion in media and the music industry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Be aware of and consider the patterns and ongoing implications of technological, cultural and economic forces which have shaped the media and music industry in Canada and around the world."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Interact and professionally engage with industry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Think, create and iterate in the music industry by operating at the nexus of context, skills, theory and self."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Critically recognize and analyze ethical problems to effect practical solutions within consideration of context."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Graduate Career Path Possibilities"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students develop holistic 21st-century skills and competencies necessary for the modern music industry across creativity, commerce and community. There are a variety of potential career paths available to graduates:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Business and Management: Artist management, concert promotion and production, music publishing, business development, public relations, film and television production, technology, advertising and marketing"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Musician: Recording, performing, songwriting, production, session musician, composition, film and television scoring"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Community: Education, governance, journalism, non-profit, activism, leadership"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Professional and Graduate School: Graduates will be prepared to pursue further postsecondary education, including research-based education, (including media, education, cultural studies) and professional education (including law school, MBA)"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Entrepreneurship: Students will be encouraged to pursue entrepreneurship and launch their own ventures, with support from on campus incubators such as the Transmedia Zone and the Music Den"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Liberal Studies"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students must take three lower level liberal studies courses and three upper level liberal studies courses to graduate. Students must not choose courses that are restricted for their program or major.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "lower level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_a/"
        },
        {
          "text": "upper level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_b/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Please refer to the liberal studies chapter of this calendar for more information on the Liberal Studies Policy. Further information on liberal studies can also be found at the Faculty of Arts' Liberal Studies website .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "liberal studies",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Liberal Studies website",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/content/ryerson/liberal-studies/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Table A - Lower Level Restrictions: BPM, MUS, NMA and RTA courses are not available for credit."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Table B - Upper Level Restrictions: BPM, MUS and RTA courses are not available for credit."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Minors"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students may pursue any Minor offered by Toronto Met (with some exceptions). Please refer to the Minors chapter of this calendar for further information on individual Minor requirements and exclusions.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
